	(text "Supply decoupling"
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 30.48 26.67 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.27 1.27)
			)
			(justify left top)
		)
		(uuid "3b5ed74e-2865-529b-af07-7e3385998211")
	)
	(text "Dedicated buses: ICM-45686 on hardware SPI0 (GPIO16/18/19, CS GPIO20, INT1 GPIO15, no INT2: pin 9 is CLKIN);\nLSM6DSK320X (IMU2) on hardware SPI1 (GPIO8/10/11, CS GPIO9); BMP581 on hardware I2C1 (GPIO22/23).\nAll sensors use V3V3_ANA. Existing supply decoupling is retained.\nICM-45686: C50/C52 are 100 nF X7R on VDD/VDDIO per datasheet Table 11."
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 10 143 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.1 1.1)
			)
			(justify left top)
		)
		(uuid "539f8727-3feb-5e2f-809c-3852667efb0f")
	)
	(text "U21 ICM-45686 (TDK InvenSense DS-000489 Rev 1.1, Table 10 \"Signal Descriptions\" / Figure 4 pin-out, Single\nInterface SPI mode, Figure 10): AP_CS (pin 12) = ICM_CS, AP_SCLK (13) = ICM_SCK, AP_SDA/AP_SDIO/AP_SDI (14)\n= ICM_MOSI, AP_SDO/AP_AD0 (1) = ICM_MISO. INT1 (4) = ICM_INT1. INT2/FSYNC/CLKIN (9) = ICM_CLKIN - typed\nbidirectional because FSYNC/CLKIN are host-driven inputs while INT2 is a chip output; only the CLKIN\nfunction is used here, driven by oscillator X1. VDD (8) and VDDIO (5) are both on V3V3_ANA; GND (6) is the only ground pin. Pins 2,\n3, 7, 10 and 11 (RESV) are all left No Connect: Table 10 allows No Connect / VDDIO / GND for every RESV\npin, and the Single-Interface SPI typical application schematic (Figure 10) shows all five left unterminated\n(internal pull enabled by default, per the per-pin notes in Table 10); they are only needed for the AUX1 or\nI2C-master dual-interface modes, neither of which this board uses. C50 (VDD) and C52 (VDDIO) are the 100 nF\nX7R of Table 11 \"Bill of Materials\" (C1/C2 in the datasheet) and are the WHOLE decoupling of this part: the\nBOM lists 0.1 uF per supply pin and nothing else, so there is no extra 1 uF per supply pin (no C51/C53 on top of them).\nTable 11's own note - \"use a larger bypass capacitor than 0.1 uF if power supply ripple exceeds\n50 mV peak-to-peak\" - is the only condition that would call for one; V3V3_ANA is an LDO output, not a switcher."
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 10 161.243 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.1 1.1)
			)
			(justify left top)
		)
		(uuid "62a430f1-aff6-51f4-999f-9f30d1bd07d1")
	)
	(text "R48: 10k from ICM_CS to V3V3_ANA; R51: 10k from IMU2_CS to V3V3_ANA.\nCS pull-ups hold each sensor deselected during reset. No pulls on SPI clock/data.\nICM_INT1 has its own MCU GPIO, independent of all other sensors; ICM pin 9 is CLKIN (X1), so there is no ICM INT2."
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 10 186.614 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.1 1.1)
			)
			(justify left top)
		)
		(uuid "adfc0628-b5f5-55e0-929a-bfd00741b964")
	)
	(text "Routing priority: ICM SPI, IMU2 SPI, native SD, then BMP581 I2C.\nUse a continuous ground reference; avoid switching nodes and long runs beside servo/pyro power."
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 160 143 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.1 1.1)
			)
			(justify left top)
		)
		(uuid "e46acb0e-f32a-59a9-9e5a-729a0dfbcc42")
	)
	(text "BOARD 2 - U21 ICM-45686: dedicated hardware SPI0. Powered from V3V3_ANA."
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 10 7 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 2 2)
			)
			(justify left top)
		)
		(uuid "f376ec32-5b48-519c-acbe-a4c16fcaf870")
	)
	(text "X1 HCI 1521H-32K000J18DTSL 32.000 kHz CMOS oscillator (LCSC C19674133) drives U21 pin 9 (CLKIN);\n32.000 kHz gives the nominal ODRs. Datasheet: HCI 1521H family (datasheets/xtal32000.pdf).\nVcc (pin 4) and E/D (pin 1, tri-state enable, always enabled) are on V3V3_ANA; C1 is 100 nF on Vcc.\nSupply build unconfirmed: the '18' ordering code may denote HCI's 1.8 V build; confirm the 3.3 V\nrating with HCI before ordering (owner decision 2026-10-26).\nNo series or pull resistor on ICM_CLKIN. Firmware (TDK app note \"ICM-456xx External Clock Input (CLKIN)\"):\nREG_MISC1 (bank 0, 0x35) OSC_ID_OVRD = 1000b selects the external clock;\nRTC_CONFIG (0x26) RTC_MODE = 1 only together with SMC_CONTROL_0 ACCEL_LP_CLK_SEL = 1;\ndisable the pin-9 internal pull-up (IPREG_BAR_REG_62 bit 0 PADS_INT2_PE_TRIM_D2A = 0);\nnever enable INT2 as an output."
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 190 92 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1 1)
			)
			(justify left top)
		)
		(uuid "6d4c58ea-9566-5e21-83b4-d9e78adb7ebe")
	)
	(text "CS idle pull-up"
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 88.9 96.52 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.27 1.27)
			)
			(justify left top)
		)
		(uuid "f9b9710e-b3da-588a-82f8-6100b98eb207")
	)
